+          <span class="monospaced">
+           args
+          </span>
+          . Setting
+          <span class="monospaced">
+           level=30
+          </span>
+          is a known workaround for Hyper-V boot failures of Windows guests on
+  recent Intel hosts when the CPU type is
+          <span class="monospaced">
+           host
+          </span>
+          or
+          <span class="monospaced">
+           max
+          </span>
+          . The property
+  only applies for x86_64 vCPUs; it is silently ignored on other
+  architectures.
+         </p>
         </li>
        </ul>
